  "question": {
    "text": "<p>An ideal diode is connected in a circuit&nbsp;with resistance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.&nbsp;If an&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math> input signal shown in the figure is given to the circuit, then the maximum and minimum value of output voltage (without load) is<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/13c62f26-3586-4c9b-84f2-aaa89669867d-image.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 223px;\" /></p>\r",
