  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the positive half cycle, the diode is in reverse bias. Due to this there will be no current in the resistor, hence the output voltage</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>For the negative half cycle,</p><p>the potential difference across output&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>V</mi></math></p>",
